# Git commit authorship

When creating or rewriting commits in any repository for this user:

- **Author name:** `Iman Suherman`
- **Author email:** `iman.suherman@gmail.com`
- **Committer:** same as author
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers (including Cursor / `cursoragent@cursor.com`)
- **Never** change global or local `git config user.*` — pass identity per commit instead

## How to commit

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Iman Suherman" \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="iman.suherman@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Iman Suherman" \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="iman.suherman@gmail.com" \
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Commit message here.

EOF
)"
```

## If Cursor injects Co-authored-by

Strip it before push. Prefer `git commit-tree` + `git reset --soft` (avoids prepare-commit-msg hooks) over `commit --amend`, then `git push --force-with-lease` only when history rewrite was explicitly requested.
